<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lisan al-Din ibn al-Khatib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1313–1374</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ibn al-Khatib</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lisan al-Din ibn al-Khatib was a poet, historian, physician and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> under Yusuf I and Muhammad V. His works include a history of Granada and a treatise arguing that plague spread by contagion. Falling from favour, he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> in 1371, was accused of heresy and was murdered in prison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1374.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-al-khatib.jpg" alt="Lisan al-Din ibn al-Khatib" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schluchtenbummler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alhambra_104.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
